From acd7e27765b84d98a11a46aca8e25c239f0d52bb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 04:14:17 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] crypto: eip93: fix request preparation and completion
 lifetime

Several request paths publish descriptors before all later DMA mappings
and the request ID have succeeded.  A later failure can then free memory
that is already owned by the packet engine.  Hash update also maps SA state
when it has no complete block to submit, leaking both mappings on its
synchronous success path.

Prepare every hash mapping and the request ID before publishing the first
descriptor.  Put the request ID on every descriptor so completion can
retain the first error when requests are interleaved.  Track mapping
ownership explicitly and use DMA_BIDIRECTIONAL for state records written
by the engine.

Fix the related cipher and AEAD error paths: free bounce buffers on every
synchronous failure, return negative DMA errors, keep the AEAD association
offset request-local, reject lengths the hardware fields cannot represent,
and reject decrypt requests shorter than their authentication tag.

Finally, cap each descriptor to its 20-bit length field and require a
32-bit DMA mask because descriptor addresses are 32 bits wide.

Fixes: 9739f5f93b78 ("crypto: eip93 - Add Inside Secure SafeXcel EIP-93 crypto engine support")
Assisted-by: Codex:gpt-5.6
Signed-off-by: Jihong Min <hurryman2212@gmail.com>
---
